    <string name="srcu_timing_headline">Run an optional local timing diagnostic</string>
    <string name="srcu_timing_detail">On supported systems this repeatedly rewrites one private dynamic permission and times how long closing a watch takes. It can slow package operations while it runs. On older or modified kernels with a known lock-inversion bug, the forced write can deadlock the system, so the device may freeze and need a forced restart; the private-process deadline cannot prevent that. Results are supporting evidence only and await device calibration.</string>
